{"kind":"assert","text":"Operator direction, hugh, 2026-08-31, relayed verbatim by checker, further refining #2193 (README agent-report prompt) and #2189 (richer local dimensions), extending assert d9ab4401: \"actually i would propose extend the timeline chart to also include annotations or symbols for significant events (data gaps, unsafe behavior etc) since that anchors much interesting investigation.\" FOR #2193: the README prompt should direct agents to make the arrival timeline the investigative anchor of the report: overlay symbols/annotations at the time of significant events - projection data gaps and stalls (the activity-stats / daily-review stops, ineffective-record bursts, partial-day boundaries), unsafe or out-of-bounds behavior (agent-guard policy_findings by severity and rule_id), repeated-failure / no-progress evidence (loop_findings by finding_kind), and harness stop/start of emission - each marker labeled and linked to the section that investigates it, so a reader can go from the mark on the timeline to the evidence. Coverage-state and partial-day annotations already present in the reference report are the model. WHAT IS DRAWABLE NOW vs NOT: policy_findings and loop_findings expose source_position but NO timestamp, and projection gaps/completeness are reported by position (tailapp health / query envelope), so at this head markers can be placed on the time axis only APPROXIMATELY by interpolating position to time through the session or harness activity span (session_progress last_source_position \u003c-\u003e last_activity_unix_nano; session_activity first/last seen). The prompt must say to label such markers as position-derived approximations. FOR #2189: to anchor markers exactly, retain an observed-time column (unix_nano of the triggering record) on policy_findings and loop_findings, and expose gap/stall/ineffective events with their observed time (and the day boundary) as a bounded queryable list, so the timeline can carry exact annotations; treat this as an operator-endorsed candidate dimension alongside the per-session time buckets in d9ab4401. Not a new request; fold into the existing two commitments and cite this assert."}